[38;2;124;124;124m**Step 2: The truth of every variable-free sentence is decidable.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mEvery ground term (built from 0, 1, +, ·) evaluates to a specific natural [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mnumber. This evaluation is effective: we can compute the value of any ground [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mterm by recursively evaluating subterms. Given the values of $t_1$ and $t_2$, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthe truth of $t_1 = t_2$ and $t_1 < t_2$ in $\mathbb{N}$ is decidable by direct [0m[38;2;124;124;124mcomparison. The truth of a Boolean combination of decidable statements is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdecidable. Therefore, there is an algorithm that, given any variable-free [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msentence $\sigma$, determines whether $\mathbb{N} \models \sigma$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Step 3: G(S) is recursive.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mA Gödel numbering $G$ is by definition an effective (computable) encoding: there[0m[38;2;124;124;124mis an algorithm that computes $G(\sigma)$ from $\sigma$, and an algorithm that, [0m[38;2;124;124;124mgiven $n$, determines whether $n$ is the Gödel number of some sentence and, if [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mso, recovers that sentence. [0m

[38;2;124;124;124mGiven $n$, we can decide membership in $G(S)$ as follows:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1. Check whether $n$ is the Gödel number of a sentence $\sigma$ (computable, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msince $G$ is effective).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. Check whether $\sigma$ is variable-free (a syntactic property, decidable by [0m
[38;2;124;124;124minspection of the parse tree).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m3. If $\sigma$ is variable-free, compute its truth value in $\mathbb{N}$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(decidable by Step 2).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m4. $n \in G(S)$ iff $\sigma$ is a variable-free true sentence.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is a decision procedure, so $G(S)$ is recursive (computable).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Step 4: Every recursive set is definable in PA.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis is a fundamental theorem of mathematical logic (the Representability [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mTheorem). It states:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m*For every recursive relation $R \subseteq \mathbb{N}^k$, there exists a formula[0m[38;2;124;124;124m$\varphi(x_1, \ldots, x_k)$ in the language of PA such that:*[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- *If $R(n_1, \ldots, n_k)$ holds, then $\text{PA} \vdash \varphi(\bar{n}_1, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\ldots, \bar{n}_k)$.*[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- *If $\neg R(n_1, \ldots, n_k)$, then $\text{PA} \vdash \neg \varphi(\bar{n}_1,[0m[38;2;124;124;124m\ldots, \bar{n}_k)$.*[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIn particular, for every recursive set $A \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, there is a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mformula $\varphi(x)$ such that for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$: $n \in A \iff [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\text{PA} \vdash \varphi(\bar{n})$, and $n \notin A \iff \text{PA} \vdash \neg [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\varphi(\bar{n})$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis implies $n \in A \iff \mathbb{N} \models \varphi(\bar{n})$, so $A$ is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdefinable in the standard model by a formula of PA, and moreover $A$ is strongly[0m[38;2;124;124;124mrepresented in PA.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe proof of the Representability Theorem proceeds by showing that PA can [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mrepresent all primitive recursive functions (via the β-function lemma and coding[0m[38;2;124;124;124mof sequences), and since every recursive function can be expressed using [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mprimitive recursive functions plus minimization (and PA can handle the relevant [0m[38;2;124;124;124mexistential quantification), all recursive relations are representable.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Step 5: Conclusion.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince $G(S)$ is recursive (Step 3) and every recursive set is definable in PA [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(Step 4), $G(S)$ is definable in PA. $\blacksquare$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Remark on "arbitrary Gödel numbering":** The result holds for any Gödel [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mnumbering $G$ in the standard sense (i.e., any effective/computable encoding). [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mThe definability of $G(S)$ in PA does not depend on the specific choice of $G$, [0m[38;2;124;124;124monly on the fact that $G$ is computable, which is part of the definition of a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mGödel numbering.[0m

